   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6pcX",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I came to New Zealand at 14, and this country gave me a life I could never have imagined. I helped build Canva from 25 employees into a global company, then came home to invest in Kiwi founders. Now I want to give back at scale. Tāmaki deserves an MP who lives here, who knows how jobs and growth are actually created, and who will fight for infrastructure matching intensification, safe streets and real opportunity."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6peS",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I'm the only candidate who lives in the electorate and our beaches, streets and schools are my daily life, not talking points. I've spent my career building things: the first Head of People at Canva, executive roles at Airtasker and Simply Wall St, and now CEO of Phase One Ventures mentoring Kiwi founders. I know how to listen, build teams and deliver to complex goals. I'll be a practical, ambitious, relentlessly local voice in Parliament."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6pgN",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Stand up for infrastructure that keeps pace with Tāmaki's growth, the pipes, roads and schools."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6piI",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Back more frontline police for public transport services keeping Tāmaki families safe."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6pkD",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Back our youth and entrepreneurs so that we have an even more powerful economy that delivers."
     }
    ],
